  "lineage": "Electronic dance music and dance craze from Davao City, named from Bisaya slang for a slacker or idle youth, built on house music and the tangonggo rhythms of the Sama-Bajau. Sherwin Tuna (DJ Love), a choreographer working in an internet cafe, turned the street dance into a musical genre in the late 2000s, producing tracks and remixes on home computer software for neighbourhood dance crews. The DAW source cards stand in for that software production.",
